/T (Despite the strong phenotypic association of CUX1 with developmental delay and intellectual disability, the homozygous state of the identified variant is not fully consistent with the established haploinsufficiency mechanism of CUX1-related neurodevelopmental disorder. Therefore, a de novo event should also be considered and, if parental samples are available, parental testing would be important to determine whether the variant is absent in both parents. Confirmation of a de novo occurrence could provide additional evidence for pathogenicity; however, the unusual zygosity would still require careful interpretation. )
/E (Despite the strong phenotypic association of CUX1 with developmental delay and intellectual disability, the homozygous state of the identified variant is not fully consistent with the established haploinsufficiency mechanism of CUX1-related neurodevelopmental disorder. Therefore, a de novo event should also be considered and, if parental samples are available, parental testing would be important to determine whether the variant is absent in both parents. Confirmation of a de novo occurrence could provide additional evidence for pathogenicity; however, the unusual zygosity would still require careful interpretation. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
